A thread another core runs is stopped without that core trapping first.
It runs on while a watcher reads its frame, and while its memory may go;
a core runs user mode only for a thread that may run, and is marked only once it has trapped.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: a core is to drop a trap it is not taking
Witness: fuzz-smp2 cores-resume-before-trap

diff --git a/kernel/core.c b/kernel/core.c
--- a/kernel/core.c
+++ b/kernel/core.c
@@ -160,9 +160,6 @@ bool core_thread_stopped(const struct thread *t)
             c->drop_trap = true;
             marked = true;
         }
-        if (c->current == t) {
-            core_shoot(c);
-        }
     }
     return marked;
 #else
